---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../../consts';
import diagram from '../../assets/build-from-scratch/transformer-complete-dimensions.png';

const codeBase =
	'https://github.com/rangarajp/rangarajp.github.io/blob/main/notebooks/transformers';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={`Transformer from Scratch - ${SITE_TITLE}`}
			description="Build an English-to-French Transformer encoder-decoder from scratch in PyTorch."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<article class="prose">
				<header class="article-header">
					<nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
						<a href="/build-from-scratch">Build from Scratch</a>
						<span class="separator">/</span>
						<span aria-current="page">Transformer</span>
					</nav>
					<a href="/build-from-scratch" class="back-link">&larr; Build from Scratch</a>
					<h1>Transformer from Scratch</h1>
					<p class="description">
						A PyTorch English→French sequence-to-sequence Transformer matching the
						original paper dimensions.
					</p>
				</header>

				<p>
					Theory lives under
					<a href="/concepts/transformers">Concepts → Transformers</a>. This page walks
					the runnable implementation in
					<code>notebooks/transformers/</code>.
				</p>

				<figure>
					<Image
						src={diagram}
						alt="Transformer architecture with expanded multi-head attention and tensor dimensions"
						widths={[800, 1200, 1600]}
						sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 900px"
					/>
					<figcaption>
						Encoder–decoder flow with expanded multi-head attention. Shapes assume
						batch=128, sequence=100, d_model=512, heads=8.
					</figcaption>
				</figure>

				<h2>What you build</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>Word-level tokenizers for English and French (OPUS Books)</li>
					<li>Encoder–decoder Transformer with 6 layers, 8 heads, d_model=512</li>
					<li>Padding masks (encoder + cross-attention) and causal masks (decoder self-attention)</li>
					<li>Training loop with validation loss and per-epoch checkpoints</li>
				</ul>

				<h2>1. Config</h2>
				<p>
					Hyperparameters and checkpoint paths live in
					<a href={`${codeBase}/config.py`}>config.py</a>:
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li><code>batch_size=128</code>, <code>seq_len=100</code></li>
					<li><code>d_model=512</code>, <code>n_heads=8</code>, <code>n_layers=6</code></li>
					<li><code>lang_src='en'</code>, <code>lang_tgt='fr'</code></li>
				</ul>

				<h2>2. Dataset and masks</h2>
				<p>
					<a href={`${codeBase}/dataset.py`}>dataset.py</a> builds fixed-length sequences
					and attention masks:
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li>
						<strong>Encoder input:</strong> <code>&lt;sos&gt; … tokens … &lt;eos&gt;</code> + pad
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Decoder input:</strong> <code>&lt;sos&gt; … tokens</code> + pad (teacher forcing)
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Label:</strong> tokens + <code>&lt;eos&gt;</code> + pad
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Encoder mask:</strong> padding only → <code>(batch, 1, 1, seq_len)</code>
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Decoder mask:</strong> padding <em>and</em> causal lower-triangular →
						<code>(batch, 1, seq_len, seq_len)</code>
					</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					Causal masking is what stops the decoder from attending to future target tokens
					during training.
				</p>

				<h2>3. Model</h2>
				<p>
					<a href={`${codeBase}/model.py`}>model.py</a> stacks the paper blocks with explicit
					shapes in comments:
				</p>
				<ol>
					<li>Input / output embeddings scaled by √d_model</li>
					<li>Sinusoidal positional encoding</li>
					<li>
						Multi-head attention: <code>Wq</code>, <code>Wk</code>, <code>Wv</code>, concat, then
						<code>Wo</code>
					</li>
					<li>Encoder layers: self-attention + FFN with residual + LayerNorm</li>
					<li>
						Decoder layers: masked self-attention → cross-attention (Q from decoder, K/V from
						encoder memory) → FFN
					</li>
					<li>Final linear projection + log-softmax over the target vocabulary</li>
				</ol>
				<p>
					Cross-attention does <strong>not</strong> reuse encoder <code>Wk</code>/<code>Wv</code>.
					Each decoder cross-attention block projects the shared encoder output with its own
					<code>Wk</code> and <code>Wv</code>.
				</p>

				<h2>4. Training</h2>
				<p>
					<a href={`${codeBase}/train.py`}>train.py</a> wires everything together:
				</p>
				<ol>
					<li>Load <code>Helsinki-NLP/opus_books</code> (<code>en-fr</code>)</li>
					<li>Build or reuse WordLevel tokenizers</li>
					<li>90/10 train–val split</li>
					<li>Adam + NLLLoss (pad ignored) + gradient clipping</li>
					<li>Save weights each epoch under <code>weights/</code></li>
				</ol>
				<pre><code>cd notebooks/transformers
python train.py</code></pre>

				<h2>Code index</h2>
				<ul>
					<li><a href={`${codeBase}/config.py`}>config.py</a> — hyperparameters</li>
					<li><a href={`${codeBase}/dataset.py`}>dataset.py</a> — batching and masks</li>
					<li><a href={`${codeBase}/model.py`}>model.py</a> — architecture</li>
					<li><a href={`${codeBase}/train.py`}>train.py</a> — training loop</li>
					<li>
						<a href={`${codeBase}/transformer-dimensions.drawio`}>transformer-dimensions.drawio</a>
						— editable dimension diagram
					</li>
				</ul>

				<p>
					For the mental model behind each block, start at
					<a href="/concepts/transformers">Transformers Overview</a>.
				</p>
			</article>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.article-header {
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
		padding-bottom: 1.5rem;
		border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
	}
	.breadcrumbs {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.35rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
	}
	.breadcrumbs a {
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
		text-decoration: none;
	}
	.breadcrumbs a:hover {
		color: var(--accent);
	}
	.separator {
		color: rgb(var(--gray-light));
	}
	.back-link {
		display: inline-block;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
		text-decoration: none;
	}
	.back-link:hover {
		color: var(--accent);
	}
	.article-header h1 {
		font-size: 2.4rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}
	.description {
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
		margin: 0;
	}
	.prose {
		line-height: 1.8;
	}
	.prose :global(h2) {
		font-size: 1.5rem;
		margin-top: 2.5rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
		font-weight: 700;
	}
	.prose :global(ol),
	.prose :global(ul) {
		padding-left: 1.5rem;
	}
	.prose :global(li) {
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}
	.prose :global(pre) {
		background-color: rgb(var(--gray-dark));
		color: #f8f8f2;
		padding: 1.25rem;
		border-radius: 8px;
		overflow-x: auto;
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		line-height: 1.5;
	}
	.prose :global(code) {
		font-size: 0.9em;
	}
	.prose :global(figure) {
		margin: 1.75rem 0;
	}
	.prose :global(img) {
		width: 100%;
		height: auto;
		border: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
		border-radius: 8px;
	}
	.prose :global(figcaption) {
		margin-top: 0.5rem;
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
	}
</style>
